For further information aids and accommodations contact the city clerk at 781-393-2425.

22
00:01:03,782 --> 00:01:10,429
So we met the subcommittee for climate sustainability and transportation met on this paper, about a month ago.

23
00:01:16,915 --> 00:01:19,758
We have the draft ordinance from KP law that we reviewed.

24
00:01:19,778 --> 00:01:21,419
I can share that on my screen.

25
00:01:22,099 --> 00:01:23,881
We did not have any formal motions.

26
00:01:24,101 --> 00:01:34,069
We and the subcommittee felt that it was in a position that we wanted to move forward that draft ordinance to get feedback from the full council and any motions to adjust it there.

27
00:01:34,509 --> 00:01:42,055
And we did have building commissioner Moki join us last time to just give us some insight as far as enforcement around this.

28
00:01:42,095 --> 00:01:45,017
And he does believe it is something that they have the,

29
00:01:46,299 --> 00:01:48,041
with people power to enforce at this time.

30
00:01:48,481 --> 00:02:01,252
So I left him off this meeting, but I'm always happy to circle him in for more, any feedback or have him come to a future meeting, but I figured since we already got that information from him, we didn't have to take another night away from him.

31
00:02:02,162 --> 00:02:07,903
And now we do have KP Law Attorney Janelle Austin, as well as DPW Commissioner Tim McGivern with us.

32
00:02:08,323 --> 00:02:22,686
Councilor Scarpelli raised last time a number of questions that he felt that DPW Commissioner McGivern may be able to answer for us around battery usage and just kind of commonplace usage within the city departments as far as leaf blowers.

33
00:02:23,106 --> 00:02:30,547
So unless other councilors would like to start with discussion or questions, I'm happy to share my screen and kind of go through

34
00:02:31,287 --> 00:02:35,571
The ordinance language and just highlight the salient points as we've had this in our inbox.

35
00:02:36,331 --> 00:02:38,593
I think since last month and was sent around again today.

36
00:02:43,357 --> 00:02:44,458
And I will share my screen then.

37
00:02:56,928 --> 00:02:58,669
So before we have the draft ordinance,

38
00:03:00,815 --> 00:03:11,645
There was some questions at the subcommittee just in this definitions portion, I think, particularly as far as the commercial leaf blower operator as there are some solo.

39
00:03:13,047 --> 00:03:22,516
There are some kind of one man band operations that may be subject to these regulations, if we wanted to adjust that from a two person two person plus organization to.

40
00:03:23,353 --> 00:03:25,915
anyone running a commercial operation.

41
00:03:27,036 --> 00:03:38,144
Leaf blowers does reference, include both battery and electric powered, I'm sorry, gas, battery and electric powered leaf blowers as far as the language of this ordinance goes.

42
00:03:39,478 --> 00:03:56,010
And the main limitations around use reference are noise ordinance that already exists, as well as limitations that leaf blowers, use of leaf blowers is prohibited except for between March 15th and May 31st and October 1st and December 15th in any year.

43
00:03:57,051 --> 00:04:02,295
It also exempts city parks and a number of city properties from these regulations.

44
00:04:04,326 --> 00:04:09,550
It further prohibits the use of leaf blowers except between the hours of nine to five Monday through Saturday.

45
00:04:09,570 --> 00:04:13,513
And it also prohibits the use on holidays.

46
00:04:14,914 --> 00:04:17,356
Again, the city properties are exempt from this.

47
00:04:19,118 --> 00:04:21,399
Then section three requests that

48
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:33,164
those who are either owners of large parcels, which is a small number for Medford, or have the commercial operation to register with the city and provide a plan.

49
00:04:34,584 --> 00:04:47,849
And then also just some general language around use as far as leaf blower operations shall not cause leaves, dirt, dust, rodent, dog or cat feces, debris, glass clippings, cuttings or trimmings from trees or shrubs or any other type to litter or debris.

50
00:04:48,343 --> 00:04:52,548
to be blown or deposited on any adjacent property or any other parcel of land.

51
00:04:53,543 --> 00:04:59,284
So just mitigating that, you know, the actual blowing of things on other properties that may be detrimental.

52
00:05:00,044 --> 00:05:11,187
And then also going into referencing the decibels once again, as well as number six on parcels of 10,000 square feet or less, only one leaf blower at a time may be used.

53
00:05:12,367 --> 00:05:18,248
And then on parcels larger than 10,000 square feet, only one leaf blower may be used within each 10,000 square foot area.

54
00:05:19,750 --> 00:05:32,394
And then also the limitation set forth in the to be numbered subsections shall not apply to de minimis use of a leaf blower by an individual on the property in which they reside, provided that such use is in compliance with the noise ordinance.

55
00:05:32,514 --> 00:05:36,535
For the subsection de minimis shall mean not more than an aggregate of five minutes per day.

56
00:05:36,555 --> 00:05:40,436
It references the enforcement authorities.

57
00:05:40,576 --> 00:05:47,918
As I said, Commissioner Mokey was fine with the code enforcement building department being the enforcement authority and did recommend

58
00:05:48,951 --> 00:05:52,453
seeing if the health department would work in concert as well.

59
00:05:53,434 --> 00:05:55,155
So we could also loop them in at a future date.

60
00:05:56,075 --> 00:06:01,079
And so those are the general overview of the health department.

61
00:06:02,448 --> 00:06:03,769
what this ordinance entails.

62
00:06:04,690 --> 00:06:06,551
Again, we didn't make any motions at the subcommittee.

63
00:06:06,671 --> 00:06:09,494
Again, we did have some questions just regarding the definitions.

64
00:06:10,374 --> 00:06:19,121
And there was some discussion among residents as far as the duration for which leaf lowers would be permitted to be used.

65
00:06:19,962 --> 00:06:25,707
So I'm happy to open it up to questions from counselors at this point.

66
00:06:26,727 --> 00:06:27,348
Councilor Collins.

67
00:06:29,745 --> 00:06:31,466
Thank you, President Morrell for that overview.

68
00:06:31,486 --> 00:06:40,493
I do have some more substantial motions that I'd like to discuss later in the meeting, but for now, I just had a couple of clarifying questions about this draft.

69
00:06:40,653 --> 00:06:43,896
Going back to that section, I think it's section seven on de minimis use.

70
00:06:43,976 --> 00:06:47,578
I just wanted to make sure I understood what this section was referring to.

71
00:06:47,638 --> 00:06:58,767
Does that mean if a leaf blower is used on a property very minimally, so for less than five minutes per day, then it's not subject to the same noise regulations and seasonal regulations?

72
00:06:59,944 --> 00:07:01,185
That was my understanding.

73
00:07:01,465 --> 00:07:03,647
Attorney Austin, if you're able to speak to that.

74
00:07:03,667 --> 00:07:07,130
Thank you, Council President Morelle.

75
00:07:07,270 --> 00:07:08,431
That is correct.

76
00:07:08,471 --> 00:07:15,336
It would basically exempt individualized use for a very narrow specific timeframe.

77
00:07:15,996 --> 00:07:22,541
And certainly that can be adjusted if the council feels as a matter of policy, it wishes to make the adjustment.

78
00:07:22,601 --> 00:07:27,085
This is consistent with other communities and how they have regulated the use

79
00:07:27,785 --> 00:07:35,951
you know, across the state to allow individuals to use it on the property themselves for non-commercial use, Councilor Collins.

80
00:07:36,011 --> 00:07:36,411
Thank you.

81
00:07:38,613 --> 00:07:38,933
Great.

82
00:07:39,273 --> 00:07:41,615
Thank you so much for that confirmation.

83
00:07:42,716 --> 00:07:45,418
And then one other clarifying question, if I may.

84
00:07:46,298 --> 00:07:55,305
Jumping up to, I want to say, section B3, I was just hoping for a little bit more clarification on the permitting process and what that

85
00:07:56,158 --> 00:07:58,779
what that would create.

86
00:07:58,819 --> 00:08:11,325
Does that mean that if a commercial operator or the owner of a large property submits and gets approved this mitigation plan, in that case, they are allowed to go outside the seasonal windows?

87
00:08:11,425 --> 00:08:13,086
Is that what this section outlines?

88
00:08:16,228 --> 00:08:17,828
Attorney Austin, if you're able to speak to that.

89
00:08:18,509 --> 00:08:18,829
Sure.

90
00:08:20,009 --> 00:08:24,272
In my opinion, that subsection three provision would exempt

91
00:08:25,810 --> 00:08:38,577
exempt if there is a permit or permission given, it would not, the prohibition would then not apply given that the entity has gone through the permitting process with the approval of the city.

92
00:08:38,717 --> 00:08:39,798
So yes, it would exempt.

93
00:08:42,019 --> 00:08:48,163
As long as there was a valid operations landline record with the city that was approved by the building commissioner or designee.

94
00:08:48,183 --> 00:08:51,865
Great, thank you again for confirming.

95
00:08:52,505 --> 00:08:53,526
Thank you, Councilor Collins.

96
00:08:56,932 --> 00:08:59,713
Any other questions from counselors?

97
00:09:00,713 --> 00:09:03,635
If I actually just could, I just have a follow-up question to that, Attorney Austin.

98
00:09:03,675 --> 00:09:11,117
So would it then be that the idea is that these plans would be submitted and that would cover an entire season of use?

99
00:09:11,197 --> 00:09:15,039
It wouldn't be a single one-off use under Section B3?

100
00:09:19,018 --> 00:09:29,284
It could be done on a, I think that that provision contemplates that regulations will be adopted and certainly it could be a seasonal or yearly basis.

101
00:09:29,965 --> 00:09:43,633
