118
00:11:09,715 --> 00:11:13,839
It is March 15th through May 31st and October 1st through December 15th.

119
00:11:22,288 --> 00:11:23,789
those dates pretty much nail it.

120
00:11:24,069 --> 00:11:28,013
So for example, you know, we just got finished with our big spring cleanup.

121
00:11:28,894 --> 00:11:30,595
So just last week.

122
00:11:31,196 --> 00:11:34,299
So that fits in that first timeframe.

123
00:11:34,339 --> 00:11:42,226
And then in the fall, I don't know off the top of my head, but I believe November, early November is our big sweep.

124
00:11:42,506 --> 00:11:43,507
So we'll try to clean up the,

125
00:11:44,343 --> 00:11:51,068
the leaves there, but the timeframe of October to December 13th, yeah, that would be Primo leaf cleanup time.

126
00:11:51,308 --> 00:11:56,611
So I don't think, unless you want to narrow these down, I think these ranges are appropriate.

127
00:11:57,012 --> 00:12:03,436
From our operations standpoint, I can get you detailed information, but I can tell you, we just finished a big spring cleanup.

128
00:12:05,097 --> 00:12:05,438
Thank you.

129
00:12:05,758 --> 00:12:10,081
I would be curious as to, I mean, if this is reasonable,

130
00:12:10,843 --> 00:12:11,844
fully happy to accept it.

131
00:12:12,984 --> 00:12:16,606
I know there is some desire for us to maybe shorten it a little bit.

132
00:12:18,247 --> 00:12:23,349
