144
00:13:16,559 --> 00:13:18,182
Those are some questions that I had as well.

145
00:13:20,543 --> 00:13:31,250
So yeah, I wanted to move on from some of my clarifying questions on the ordinance to sort of considering it a bit more broadly, a bit more sort of the opportunity this ordinance presents.

146
00:13:33,592 --> 00:13:40,016
I love the regulations that this ordinance lays out regarding seasonal effective dates, noise regulation.

147
00:13:40,056 --> 00:13:44,219
I think that these are issues that I personally have heard from a lot of constituents about.

148
00:13:46,400 --> 00:13:48,802
I also think that this is an opportunity to consider

149
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:52,862
phasing out the use of gas-powered leaf blowers entirely.

150
00:13:53,102 --> 00:14:11,071
So something that I've heard from several constituents about while this was working its way through the subcommittee, the environmental impacts of gas-powered leaf blowers are extensively documented, local air pollution, creation of ozone, all these factors that exacerbate climate change.

151
00:14:11,091 --> 00:14:14,353
I was reading something that said that sort of pound for pound,

152
00:14:14,810 --> 00:14:18,012
these gas powered leaf blowers are more polluting than cars even.

153
00:14:18,613 --> 00:14:24,597
So I think that this poses a chance for us to be a real, a leader on mitigating the causes of climate change.

154
00:14:25,858 --> 00:14:42,390
And so I'd love for us to discuss if this could be an opportunity to phase out their use entirely, you know, considering the polystyrene ban ordinance that this council recently discussed, you know, similar to that, I think that there's a way that we could do this in a way that gives property owners

155
00:14:43,018 --> 00:14:53,127
commercial operators ample time to prepare for phasing out, you know, perhaps even an opportunity to defer effective date again like we did with the polystyrene ban.

156
00:14:53,147 --> 00:15:01,755
You know, with the ongoing supply chain issues which I'm sure is affecting the lawn care supplies industry as it is almost every other industry.

157
00:15:03,988 --> 00:15:13,215
I think that this is something that for environmental and public health reasons, I'd love for this council to consider to make this ordinance even stronger, even more protective of public health.

158
00:15:13,936 --> 00:15:22,222
And at the same time, balance that with not forcing property owners and commercial operators to turn on a dime and have their business impacted.

159
00:15:23,443 --> 00:15:33,571
So for that reason, I'd like to make the motion to have our council provide draft language on a phased in prohibition

160
00:15:34,788 --> 00:15:37,909
on gas-powered leaf blowers to add to this ordinance.

161
00:15:41,629 --> 00:15:42,390
Thank you, Councilor Collins.

162
00:15:42,410 --> 00:15:43,770
Do I have a second on that motion?

163
00:15:43,790 --> 00:15:52,731
I would second it if the Councilor would be amenable to amending it, that the phase-in would occur over two years.

164
00:15:53,552 --> 00:15:55,152
That was exactly what I had in mind.

165
00:15:56,312 --> 00:15:57,672
Great, then I second it.

166
00:15:59,453 --> 00:16:00,373
Thank you, Councilor Collins.

167
00:16:01,113 --> 00:16:01,553
Councilor Knight.

168
00:16:02,938 --> 00:16:04,139
Madam President, thank you very much.

169
00:16:04,799 --> 00:16:10,263
