00:19:04,154 --> 00:19:06,476
I said, I said, thank you very much, Madam President.

213
00:19:06,556 --> 00:19:06,936
Sorry.

214
00:19:07,437 --> 00:19:07,877
Thank you.

215
00:19:07,897 --> 00:19:08,678
That was a short one.

216
00:19:08,698 --> 00:19:09,659
That was a short one for me.

217
00:19:09,679 --> 00:19:09,959
I know.

218
00:19:12,040 --> 00:19:12,861
Vice President Behrs.

219
00:19:13,622 --> 00:19:14,682
Thank you, Madam President.

220
00:19:17,104 --> 00:19:26,972
I had kind of five items relevant to this relative to this draft, maybe a sixth after further reading during this meeting.

221
00:19:28,033 --> 00:19:31,896
One was, I think there should be a prompt and permanent phase out of gas powered leaf blowers.

222
00:19:33,366 --> 00:19:39,030
and I think we now have a motion and a second to get some draft language around that.

223
00:19:40,291 --> 00:19:45,075
And I do know that we were already holding the city to that standard and I think we should hold everyone else to that same standard.

224
00:19:47,997 --> 00:19:53,862
Restrictions on the time of day, I think that makes sense as well, nine to five, which is currently written here.

225
00:19:55,043 --> 00:20:00,807
In terms of the times of year, I'm okay with the ones that are in here, although I do think that December 1st to December 15th

226
00:20:02,120 --> 00:20:10,945
is generally a little bit late in the season for leaf removal, at least where we are in North Medford.

227
00:20:11,005 --> 00:20:18,148
But I'd be open to a discussion around that, especially maybe a little bit of a shortening of the fall end of it.

228
00:20:20,665 --> 00:20:36,797
One thing that I saw, you know, I think we got it pretty close to right on restricting how many leaf blowers can be running at the same time on a single property, but I didn't see addressed was how long they can be constantly making noise on a single property.

229
00:20:38,018 --> 00:20:47,506
I'd like to make a motion that we have language to limit them from consistently being on for more than one hour per day.

230
00:20:47,526 --> 00:20:48,086
Now, so if,

231
00:20:49,803 --> 00:20:58,348
someone uses it for 15 minutes here, 10 minutes there, five minutes there, that would be different.

232
00:20:58,368 --> 00:21:06,252
But I think one of the issues is just when it's the constant droning and noise for an hour or an hour and a half, that that's very disruptive.

233
00:21:06,412 --> 00:21:14,596
So the motion would be to limit constant use to one hour per day per property.

234
00:21:14,616 --> 00:21:17,518
Okay.

235
00:21:18,099 --> 00:21:19,200
Point of information, Madam President.

236
00:21:19,961 --> 00:21:21,042
Point of information, Councilor Knight.

237
00:21:21,982 --> 00:21:25,485
Don't we have a noise ordinance already that would address the constant droning and nuisance ordinance?

238
00:21:29,969 --> 00:21:32,131
I will check on that.

239
00:21:33,112 --> 00:21:42,020
From my reading of the committee report, I didn't capture that Commissioner Moki felt that that would be something they could enforce, but yeah.

240
00:21:42,447 --> 00:21:44,428
but that's just my reading of it.

241
00:21:44,749 --> 00:21:48,171
If it is, then I don't think it would need to be included in this ordinance.

242
00:21:49,292 --> 00:21:50,212
I just referenced it, you know?

243
00:21:51,193 --> 00:21:51,413
Yeah.

244
00:21:55,696 --> 00:21:59,299
Do I have a second for Councilor, Vice-President Bear's motion?

245
00:22:00,399 --> 00:22:08,065
And before I, given Councilor Nye's point, I'll amend the motion to say either draft language pending

246
00:22:10,128 --> 00:22:14,130
request to the building commissioner as to whether the noise ordinance would already cover that.

247
00:22:14,910 --> 00:22:18,092
We got a lawyer here we're paying $65,000 so we can have them research it.

248
00:22:18,192 --> 00:22:20,913
Oh yeah, yeah, sure.

249
00:22:20,993 --> 00:22:22,214
That makes that makes sense.

250
00:22:22,234 --> 00:22:22,874
I'm fine with that.

251
00:22:23,135 --> 00:22:30,238
We'll ask KP a lot of just see if this already is covered in the noise ordinance and if not, then to draft language to include it in this ordinance.

252
00:22:37,540 --> 00:22:40,142
Okay, do I have a second on a vices and bears motion.

253
00:22:40,942 --> 00:22:45,685
Second, because they're saying, and you had more vices and bears.

254
00:22:46,446 --> 00:22:51,809
Yeah, I have some serious problems about section B three.

255
00:22:54,191 --> 00:23:02,596
At the very least, I think we should update the definition of commercially floor to include those single operators as was previously mentioned.

256
00:23:05,445 --> 00:23:12,773
And I think at the end of the day, most of the issues that folks have around this are with commercial operators.

257
00:23:13,954 --> 00:23:24,124
I don't see residents out every week for multiple hours a day with multiple leaf blowers, creating lots of noise and pollution in our neighborhoods.

258
00:23:24,204 --> 00:23:27,547
But I do think that's what the commercial operators are doing.

259
00:23:29,063 --> 00:23:46,557
So I don't have a motion on this right now but I'm personally reticent to create a separate set of standards for people who are doing this for profit and have an incentive to minimize the time that they spend

260
00:23:48,253 --> 00:23:53,756
cleaning a property and maximize the revenue that they're gaining from it.

261
00:23:54,737 --> 00:23:58,118
I think that sets them apart from a resident maintaining their own property.

262
00:23:58,138 --> 00:24:03,401
I think that sets them apart from our DPW maintaining public property.

263
00:24:03,541 --> 00:24:06,483
So I'm just putting that out there for further discussion.

264
00:24:08,624 --> 00:24:10,065
You know, I think we'll be coming back

265
00:24:11,456 --> 00:24:12,517
and discussing this again.

266
00:24:12,537 --> 00:24:21,608
And I may make a motion at a later time, but maybe that's something to discuss after we have some commercial operators invited.

267
00:24:21,628 --> 00:24:24,712
But I just want to put that out into a discussion.

268
00:24:25,013 --> 00:24:26,134
So that's all I have.

269
00:24:26,214 --> 00:24:26,635
Thank you.

270
00:24:26,655 --> 00:24:28,377
Thank you.

271
00:24:28,417 --> 00:24:30,259
I would agree with you there because it does seem like

272
00:24:30,746 --> 00:24:39,333
In my opinion, we're putting this effort into these regulations and that number three, B3 kind of invalidates all of them if you submit a plan.

273
00:24:39,353 --> 00:24:41,415
And I think that's great.

274
00:24:41,435 --> 00:24:47,279
I think these plans, I think the requirements of the plan are important, but that's not what residents are asking us.

275
00:24:47,339 --> 00:24:55,806
Residents are asking us for relief from the constant noise, the constant emissions, the constant dust and debris flying into their yards and their windows.

276
00:24:56,687 --> 00:24:57,688
So I would agree with you there.

277
00:24:59,904 --> 00:25:00,544
Councilor Collins.

278
00:25:01,765 --> 00:25:02,645
Thank you, President Merrill.

279
00:25:03,005 --> 00:25:13,289
I just wanted to add my voice in a sense, you know, I think with regulations like these I do think it's important to provide for opportunities for exceptions, exemptions, where they're appropriate.

280
00:25:13,729 --> 00:25:22,312
You know, I think it's a great idea to invite the Chamber of Commerce and commercial leaf blower operators to a next meeting on this because I think it would be helpful if we could

281
00:25:22,908 --> 00:25:28,789
maybe amend this section to be a little more targeted for what those potential exceptions and exemptions could be.

282
00:25:28,829 --> 00:25:30,329
I think that you stated it well.

283
00:25:30,369 --> 00:25:43,652
I think this is kind of what I was thinking about in the question earlier is if we devise stricter regulations and then there's a permit that waives all of them, that's a pretty big wave.

284
00:25:44,272 --> 00:25:48,413
So I think that I too would be interested in discussing which

285
00:25:50,993 --> 00:25:59,440
which regulations could be important to have more wiggle room on and where maybe we could tighten this to just keep it in the spirit of the ordinance.

286
00:26:00,340 --> 00:26:00,641
Thank you.

287
00:26:01,541 --> 00:26:02,462
Thank you, Councilor Collins.

288
00:26:04,283 --> 00:26:06,105
Any further discussion from Councillors?

289
00:26:08,827 --> 00:26:11,829
I do have a few questions, Commissioner McGivern.

290
00:26:12,810 --> 00:26:19,415
Is there intent or plans or has there been just kind of fact finding around what it would cost and if

291
00:26:20,117 --> 00:26:28,641
the work could be accomplished if the city were to transition to battery or electric leaf blowers, which don't have the emissions and they tend to have much less noise as well.

292
00:26:31,462 --> 00:26:35,184
Not that I'm aware of, but I can find out if something has been done in the past.

293
00:26:35,484 --> 00:26:38,806
We also have contractors that would use leaf blowers.

294
00:26:39,446 --> 00:26:45,049
I believe industry sort of preference is still gas, you know, fuel powered.

295
00:26:46,905 --> 00:26:53,068
But yeah, I can find out if any work has been done and not that I am aware of and not since I've been at the helm.

296
00:26:54,408 --> 00:26:55,488
Thank you.

297
00:26:55,649 --> 00:27:02,871
And then also, at what regularity are our crews using leaf blowers on these parcels?

298
00:27:03,151 --> 00:27:03,612
Is it weekly?

299
00:27:03,652 --> 00:27:04,172
Is it monthly?

300
00:27:04,232 --> 00:27:08,993
I mean, I know, you know, I walk in the cemetery a lot and go to the parks and they look pretty well clean.

301
00:27:09,074 --> 00:27:12,955
So I know they're working when I'm not seeing them, but I'm just curious how often.

302
00:27:14,445 --> 00:27:16,387
Well, I'm pretty sure it's as needed.

303
00:27:16,407 --> 00:27:19,249
So we're definitely not out there every day.

304
00:27:19,549 --> 00:27:30,217
So you would probably notice in the fall, you know, probably weekly during, you know, the, the, the high fully or the high falling, you know, time period.

305
00:27:31,999 --> 00:27:36,082
But, you know, we're not, we're not going to be using leaf blowers if there's nothing to clean up.

306
00:27:36,702 --> 00:27:44,048
So, but I do know it's, it's common practice during those high intensity use time periods that, you know, we're pretty much nailed down there in the,

307
00:27:45,195 --> 00:27:46,135
in the language there, but.

308
00:27:48,356 --> 00:27:48,996
Great, thank you.

309
00:27:49,056 --> 00:27:56,578
And then this gets pun intended a little into the weeds, but I know some of the frustration residents have is the leaf blowers are used.

310
00:27:57,058 --> 00:28:01,059
They're using them to blow around lawn clippings or a little bit of dust in a driveway.

311
00:28:01,079 --> 00:28:06,541
Does the city, you know, truly use leaf blowers for blowing leaves and those cleanup times?

312
00:28:06,601 --> 00:28:09,802
Or are they used for, you know, mowing projects or other things?

313
00:28:13,541 --> 00:28:19,889
They are good tools for general cleanup of anything like grass clippings on the ground that you can blow.

314
00:28:19,909 --> 00:28:23,312
They're used for cleanup of anything like that, I would imagine.

315
00:28:23,372 --> 00:28:27,657
I don't know for sure, but I can just imagine just from my own experience and seeing crews out there.

316
00:28:27,757 --> 00:28:34,165
But primarily leaves and grass clippings, things like that.

317
00:28:35,215 --> 00:28:35,816
Okay, great.

318
00:28:35,916 --> 00:28:36,237
Thank you.

319
00:28:36,337 --> 00:28:47,272
And last question for me, and I know you're new into this role, but to your knowledge, does DPW get complaints about the use of leaf blowers in these larger, you know, in the parks and these larger parcels?

320
00:28:47,312 --> 00:28:50,357
I know this stuff tends to come from just dense neighborhoods.

321
00:28:51,972 --> 00:28:53,393
Right, I don't know the answer.

322
00:28:53,413 --> 00:29:04,984
I haven't experienced any complaints about leaf blowers directly to me or even really through the office, but I would imagine every now and then we get a complaint about something like that.

323
00:29:05,024 --> 00:29:08,487
It seems to me like one of those things that we would get complaints on at the DPW.

324
00:29:09,488 --> 00:29:16,994
I can kind of follow up and see, you know, take the temperature there on what kind of complaint level we see.

325
00:29:18,213 --> 00:29:36,078
Yeah, and I think yeah to count some nights points I think you know, holding the city to to a similar high standard I've absolutely like just, you know, looking into that and I think, like I said, I think most of us get complaints just from the neighborhood aspect, or I haven't gotten complaints regarding larger parcel parcels but it would be really helpful to have that information as we move forward.

326
00:29:36,878 --> 00:29:40,359
Do you mind if I make a comment or two.

327
00:29:42,392 --> 00:29:48,397
So I just noticed while you're passing through the ordinances that you had a bunch of parks listed there.

328
00:29:48,417 --> 00:30:02,447
And I would say, if we're going the direction of, you know, keeping this commercial in excluding city properties make sure we're including city buildings and the grounds around city buildings, as well as schools, which would be included to build this.

329
00:30:03,087 --> 00:30:04,148
They're just bigger pieces of property.

330
00:30:05,029 --> 00:30:05,649
Maybe you already did that.

331
00:30:05,669 --> 00:30:07,230
I just didn't see them in the list.

332
00:30:07,991 --> 00:30:25,284
And then I think if you were to go to the other direction and hold the city to this standard too, I would definitely want to take a closer look, be a little bit more involved, and definitely give the folks that are doing this sort of work on the ground an opportunity to comment and weigh in on this.

333
00:30:26,225 --> 00:30:31,830
So the lead of our park division, for example, Mike Nestor, he would be an excellent resource

334
00:30:32,541 --> 00:30:35,064
to help you guys out, for example.

335
00:30:35,724 --> 00:30:44,853
So I just want to put that on your radar if it does go in that direction, because we would need to, we would want to inform you and then we would want to react and plan appropriately.

336
00:30:46,034 --> 00:30:46,255
Great.

337
00:30:46,575 --> 00:30:47,476
Thank you, Commissioner McIver.

338
00:30:48,437 --> 00:30:49,458
Vice President Behrs.

339
00:30:51,180 --> 00:30:52,141
Thank you, Madam President.

340
00:30:54,103 --> 00:30:56,185
I would first happily motion that

341
00:30:57,252 --> 00:31:13,576
