342
00:31:16,897 --> 00:31:18,937
Do I have a second on vice-president Bear's motion?

343
00:31:21,298 --> 00:31:22,638
Councillor Collins on the second.

344
00:31:27,914 --> 00:31:31,375
And then I actually have a question for the commissioner.

345
00:31:33,016 --> 00:31:45,320
When city employees are contract, well, maybe you don't have as much control over contractors, but at least when city employees are using leaf blowers, do they wear hearing or respiratory protection?

346
00:31:49,861 --> 00:31:50,142
Yes.

347
00:31:50,302 --> 00:31:57,024
So if tools or equipment are, you know, have a risk of causing ear damage,

348
00:31:57,837 --> 00:32:04,662
then, you know, ear protection is worn or eye, you know, same with eye protection, same with, you know, wearing safety vests.

349
00:32:04,702 --> 00:32:09,005
So PPE, we try to make sure that we're using appropriate PPE.

350
00:32:10,527 --> 00:32:25,678
Okay, I would move that the ordinance require that commercial operators and operators on the large parcels OLP be required to

351
00:32:26,497 --> 00:32:29,598
provide effective PPE for hearing.

352
00:32:31,058 --> 00:32:32,859
Well, just let's just say effective PPE.

353
00:32:32,919 --> 00:32:37,540
And if we need to itemize that we can for their workers.

354
00:32:40,601 --> 00:32:42,701
Do I have a second on that motion from vice president bears?

355
00:32:42,721 --> 00:32:43,421
Second.

356
00:32:44,602 --> 00:32:45,782
Second from Councillor Collins.

357
00:32:48,863 --> 00:32:50,283
Any further discussion from the council?

358
00:32:54,811 --> 00:32:57,293
